0..71 Comment "// A row may name an instance of an interface by a label (#2271): `say`"
72..147 Comment "// performs `std.io.Console.Eff` through its instance `out`, apart from the"
148..222 Comment "// interface\'s default and from every other instance, so one row holds two"
223..291 Comment "// instances of one interface. The label is a parameter the function"
292..367 Comment "// abstracts, placed after every parameter it writes: a call supplies it by"
368..442 Comment "// name, `say[.out = c]()`, or omits it and passes the one instance of the"
443..518 Comment "// interface handled where the call stands, a capability scope\'s capability"
519..585 Comment "// or a label of the caller\'s own row (Brachthäuser, Schuster and"
586..657 Comment "// Ostermann, \"Effects as Capabilities: Effect Handlers and Lightweight"
658..715 Comment "// Effect Polymorphism\", OOPSLA 2020). What refuses is in"
716..770 Comment "// `../../pathological/control/named-instances.gandr`."
772..843 Comment "/// A line printed through the instance `out`, the capability its label"
844..854 Comment "/// binds."
